  "description": "A self-seeded maple tree - rear garden. approx. 7m high, trunk dia. approx. 25 cm. Approx. 5m from the house, immediately adjacent to the boundary fence, with the base of the trunk already in contact with the fence. Currently healthy. Removal during the winter using a suitably qualified and experienced tree surgeon. All works will take place within our garden. Access for the tree surgeon will be through our terraced property, which is currently undergoing renovation and has no furnished ground-floor living space. The works will not require access from or occupation of the public highway and are not expected to cause disruption to the public.",
